In article <90120.164729DN5@psuvm.psu.edu>, DN5@psuvm.psu.edu writes:

> Mac nethack, pl 7, crashes on my Mac (Mac II, 5 meg, 40 meg hard disk,
> inits: Facade, After Dark--also Moire).  I believe that these crashes are
> caused by some strange interaction with SADE.  As near as I can tell,
> they all come when nethack tries to put up a dialog box.  I had given
> nethack 1.4 and 2 meg Multifinder partitions to run in.

Strange... the Dialogs/Alerts are actually plain mac windows, with
roundRects in them. This was the easiest way to provide good keyboard
support. It reads in a resource template for each "alert" (oh, they
are so-called local-modal, i.e. you can context switch to another app,
but not continue with nethack before you've answered)

This seems _very_ strange. I don't use SADE, though (devoted TC 4 fan)
so I can't check this. Try putting a stop in MacAlert.c function
MacAlert, and step to see where it crashes (if you built the game
yourself, that is)

More reports welcome !

> Oh yeah, MultiFinder 6.1b7 and 6.1b9 (which might be the problem, but
> there have been no crashes since I stopped playing with SADE active).

Nope, it has been thoroughly hashed through the "Set Aside" MFs... We
had some problems with the window shrinking before, but that's solved
in pl7.

